1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,920
A billion dollars is so big your brain can't fucking hold it.

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:08,360
So let's shrink it. You have to spend a thousand dollars every single day.

3
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:12,460
Start with one million. You're broke in about two years and nine months.

4
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:14,640
That's less time than a car loan, by the way.

5
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:19,200
Fancy dinners, a nice car, two big trips, and poof, it's gone.

6
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:21,560
Double-tap if you'd blow it in month one.

7
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:24,700
Now do the same thing with one billion dollars.

8
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,180
A thousand a day, every day. How long does it last?

9
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:31,800
Two thousand seven hundred thirty-eight damn years.

10
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:35,460
To be broke today, you'd have started around seven hundred BC.

11
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:39,000
Ancient Rome was a tiny new town back then. Seriously.

12
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:43,820
A billion isn't ten millions, or a hundred. It's a thousand of them.

13
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:47,180
Send this to whoever thinks a billion is just a big million.

14
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:51,280
Still not feeling it? Count one number every second, no sleep.

15
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:54,280
A million seconds is about eleven and a half days.

16
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:56,460
Follow, 'cause this next one hurts.

17
00:00:56,820 --> 00:01:00,380
A billion seconds? Almost thirty-two years of your life.

18
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:03,120
That's the difference between rich and ridiculous.

19
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:07,320
So no, a billionaire isn't just a millionaire with extra steps.

20
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:10,960
Million or billion, how long would you last? One number.

